Cell["\<\
The steps are solved in order. At each step every branch is extended by every \
realisation of each construction of the step: a vertex for a point or an \
intersection, a vertex list for a segment, a ray, a line or a circle. So the \
number of branches is the product of the numbers of choices made along the \
way.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"06c38b2b-27a7-4f9d-a99a-e9a8433e453e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An object bound in ",
 StyleBox["bindings", "TI"],
 " is not constructed again, and the objects that depend on it read its fixed \
value."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6bb0ae33-cc76-4bc6-9eb3-56bc32b560ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The assertions are checked last, on the finished branches. An assertion \
whose objects are not all bound, as after a partial solve, is not checked. A \
branch whose construction has no realisation stops, so a construction that \
stalls gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb7a8ea0-c7e4-49b6-8317-a75bebbde8a1"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c5d5af66-5a42-4384-93a9-5d3273ddc78d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " counts steps, not solutions."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"808a12a7-dcd8-4455-92e0-93b2892b1f1d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<PruneProbability\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "q"}]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ebf2aec9-93e7-4441-868d-3217445494fd"],
 " drops each branch with probability ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " after every step, keeping at least one. The default is ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1681781d-bd1a-4aac-89dc-13da15a22ffb"],
 ", exhaustive. The draw is random, so put ",
 Cell[BoxData["SeedRandom"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fdab7d7a-5397-4879-9a3d-a7eec3ceeda3"],
 " in front."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f1cbf337-3632-4432-a24c-35425fa8b316"]
}, Open  ]],

